message: "If you use this research software or its evidence, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Market state versus event labels in historical analogy: a registered oil-market experiment"
authors:
  - family-names: Delany
    given-names: Joseph
    email: joseph.delany21@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Colby College"
version: "3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-03"
repository-code: "https://github.com/josephdelany/ripple-engine"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - historical analogy
  - geopolitical risk
  - oil markets
  - walk-forward evaluation
  - proper scoring rules
abstract: >-
  A registered walk-forward experiment and concentration-matched ablation compare
  recent market state with event-class matching on identical historical support.
  Across 264 forecast dates, market-state matching outperforms event class at equal
  effective sample size; sparse leadership and dyadic fields add no demonstrated
  value. The study does not establish production forecasting skill.
